note: hair_back (back hair): config.cloth."back hair" -> 2 tree(s) per side of the eye axis, from head, rooted on the eye line and tipped 4 px above its bottom, 3 link(s) each (hairback_r0_, hairback_r1_, hairback_l0_, hairback_l1_); 12 constraint(s), physics on every link, wind 1 -> 8 and gravity 4 -> 24 root to tip (multipliers of the consumer's environment; no direction is drafted), no idle key; the recipe's own defaults, measured on its synthetic fixture (AUTHORING §3): length_ratio 0.5, strength 100/100/50
note: hair_front (head:front hair): bang_r, bang_c, bang_l are a template, not its locks — columns at 0.25, 0.5 and 0.75 of the face box's width, along the head's down axis (the eye line's perpendicular, roll 4.844 degrees), each rooted on the part's art; the opaque shape does not separate the locks painted inside one mass of hair, so a lock that runs elsewhere is not followed — move the chains onto the locks
note: hair_front (head:front hair): config.cloth."front hair" -> bang_r, bang_c, bang_l carry physics on both links (bang_r and bang_l the edge's strength, bang_c the trunk's; wind and gravity on the recipe's root-to-tip ramp over their two links) and no idle key; the recipe's chains, links and split shape the hanging strands, not the fringe
note: hair_front (front hair): config.cloth."front hair" -> 1 tree(s) on the strand at x 370, from head, rooted 0.22 face heights above the eye line and tipped 5 px below the strand, 3 link(s) each (lockt0_); 4 constraint(s), physics on every link, wind 1 -> 6 and gravity 2 -> 12 root to tip (multipliers of the consumer's environment; no direction is drafted), no idle key; the recipe's own defaults, measured on its synthetic fixture (AUTHORING §3): length_ratio 0.5, strength 100/100/50
